331 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H1 /T (Q4.  Define parametric and non-parametric memory) /E (Q4.  Define parametric and non-parametric memory) /Alt () /Pg 20 0 R /K [0 ] >> endobj
332 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 200 0 R /Pg 20 0 R >> endobj
333 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H2 /T (Parametric Memory: LLMs have been demonstrated to be stores of factual knowledge. It can be said that LLMs store factual information in their parameters. This internal memory of the LLM which is influenced by the size of the model and the training data is called parametric memory. Non-Parametric Memory: Conversely, any information that is external to the LLM but can be made available via a RAG pipeline is called non-parametric information \(since it is not stored in the model parameters\). Any store of such external information forms the non-parametric memory of the system.) /E (Parametric Memory: LLMs have been demonstrated to be stores of factual knowledge. It can be said that LLMs store factual information in their parameters. This internal memory of the LLM which is influenced by the size of the model and the training data is called parametric memory. Non-Parametric Memory: Conversely, any information that is external to the LLM but can be made available via a RAG pipeline is called non-parametric information \(since it is not stored in the model parameters\). Any store of such external information forms the non-parametric memory of the system.) /Alt () /Pg 20 0 R /K [1 ] >> endobj
334 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 200 0 R /K [2 ] /Pg 20 0 R >> endobj
335 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 200 0 R /Pg 20 0 R >> endobj
