337 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 794 0 R /ActualText (Abhinav Kimothi) /Alt () /Pg 20 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
338 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H1 /T (Q5. ) /E (Q5. ) /Alt () /Pg 21 0 R /K [2 ] >> endobj
339 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 795 0 R /ActualText (What are the three core steps of RAG?) /Alt () /Pg 21 0 R /K [3 ] >> endobj
340 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 201 0 R /Pg 21 0 R >> endobj
341 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H2 /T (As the name - Retrieval Augmented Generation - suggests, there are three core steps in the RAG process -  Retrieval: Fetching relevant information, document or data from external sources based on the input query \(or prompt\). Augmentation: Incorporating the retrieved information into the input prompt. Generation: Producing the final response using the augmented prompt.) /E (As the name - Retrieval Augmented Generation - suggests, there are three core steps in the RAG process -  Retrieval: Fetching relevant information, document or data from external sources based on the input query \(or prompt\). Augmentation: Incorporating the retrieved information into the input prompt. Generation: Producing the final response using the augmented prompt.) /Alt () /Pg 21 0 R /K [1 ] >> endobj
342 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 201 0 R /K [0 ] /Pg 21 0 R >> endobj
343 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 201 0 R /Pg 21 0 R >> endobj
344 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 796 0 R /ActualText (RAG in 80 Questions) /Alt () /Pg 21 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
345 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 797 0 R /ActualText (Abhinav Kimothi) /Alt () /Pg 21 0 R /K [5 ] >> endobj
346 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H1 /T (Q6. ) /E (Q6. ) /Alt () /Pg 22 0 R /K [1 ] >> endobj
347 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 798 0 R /ActualText (How does RAG address hallucination issues in LLMs?) /Alt () /Pg 22 0 R /K [2 ] >> endobj
348 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 202 0 R /Pg 22 0 R >> endobj
349 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H2 /T (RAG mitigates hallucinations by grounding LLM outputs in factual, retrieved information from external sources, reducing the likelihood of generating incorrect or fabricated content. With this contextual awareness, the tendency of LLM responses to be factually inaccurate is greatly reduced. The LLMs, therefore, hallucinate less in RAG systems.) /E (RAG mitigates hallucinations by grounding LLM outputs in factual, retrieved information from external sources, reducing the likelihood of generating incorrect or fabricated content. With this contextual awareness, the tendency of LLM responses to be factually inaccurate is greatly reduced. The LLMs, therefore, hallucinate less in RAG systems.) /Alt () /Pg 22 0 R /K [0 ] >> endobj
350 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 202 0 R /Pg 22 0 R >> endobj
351 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 799 0 R /ActualText (RAG in 80 Questions) /Alt () /Pg 22 0 R /K [3 ] >> endobj
352 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 800 0 R /ActualText (Abhinav Kimothi) /Alt () /Pg 22 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
353 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H1 /T (Q7. ) /E (Q7. ) /Alt () /Pg 23 0 R /K [3 ] >> endobj
354 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /P /P 801 0 R /ActualText (How does RAG improve response reliability in LLMs?) /Alt () /Pg 23 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
355 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 203 0 R /Pg 23 0 R >> endobj
356 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H2 /T (The added external information assists the LLM in generating responses that are contextually appropriate and the users can be relatively more assured. For example, if the non-parametric memory contains information about a particular companys products, users can be assured that the LLM will generate responses about those products from the provided sources and not from elsewhere.) /E (The added external information assists the LLM in generating responses that are contextually appropriate and the users can be relatively more assured. For example, if the non-parametric memory contains information about a particular companys products, users can be assured that the LLM will generate responses about those products from the provided sources and not from elsewhere.) /Alt () /Pg 23 0 R /K [0 ] >> endobj
357 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H2 /T (In addition to being context aware, because the information is being fetched from a known source, these sources can be cited in the response. This makes the responses more reliable since the users have the choice of validating the information from the source.) /E (In addition to being context aware, because the information is being fetched from a known source, these sources can be cited in the response. This makes the responses more reliable since the users have the choice of validating the information from the source.) /Alt () /Pg 23 0 R /K [1 ] >> endobj
