388 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H1 /T (Q9.  difference between an LLM and a RAG system?) /E (Q9.  difference between an LLM and a RAG system?) /Alt () /Pg 27 0 R /K [1 ] >> endobj
389 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /Figure /P 207 0 R /Pg 27 0 R >> endobj
390 0 obj <</Type /StructElem /S /H2 /T (A naïve LLM relies solely on its internal knowledge, while a RAG-powered LLM integrates external information during inference, leading to more accurate and context-aware responses.) /E (A naïve LLM relies solely on its internal knowledge, while a RAG-powered LLM integrates external information during inference, leading to more accurate and context-aware responses.) /Alt () /Pg 27 0 R /K [4 ] >> endobj
